    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, the only test in the project) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), mirroring the existing helper-class design to keep structural impact low.\n\n**Changes (4 files):**\n- **`MembershipLevel.java`** (new): a small, self-contained helper \u2014 `of(namesakeCount, email)` starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: swapped the one `@Mapping` line from `membershipTier` (with its `GOLD`/household override) to `membershipLevel`, delegating to the new helper. No method body grew.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: replaced the `membershipTier` string property with `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133, readOnly), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer carries `membershipTier`.\n- **`MembershipTier.java`**: deleted, now unused (only the mapper referenced it).\n\n**On the audit line:** the spec says \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\" I verified the create audit line in `OwnerAuditListener` only logs `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate` \u2014 it never recorded the tier \u2014 so that clause is satisfied with no change needed there, avoiding an unnecessary extra file touch.\n\nThe new `coreNumericLevel` test (unique owner with email \u2192 1 + email + namesake0 = 3) passes.",
